# patches/uboot/series — quilt-style ordered apply list.
# One filename per line (relative to this dir). '#' = comment, blank lines OK.
# Applied by scripts/apply-series.sh via `git am` (run from the uboot tree).
#
# U-Boot RK3506 SoC support is ALREADY upstream (Jonas Karlman v2 merged into
# 2026.07-rc4), so this series holds ONLY the board/DT/defconfig + SFC delta.
# Regenerated 2026-06-16 from explore/uboot (base 5ca1a73c) via git format-patch.

0001-rockchip-rk3506-add-AES-RK3506B-board-support-DT-def.patch
# SFC sampling delay-line tuning — mirror of linux 0003. Without it U-Boot
# cannot read the kernel FIT from NAND (corrupt reads). U-Boot SFC runs at
# 100MHz real (rk3506_clk_set_rate ENOENT) but DLL-tuned reads are reliable.
0002-spi-rockchip_sfc-add-sampling-delay-line-tuning-for-.patch
# SFC 80MHz + rockchip,max-dll (mirror of linux 0005; board runs 50MHz in
# practice via the linux side, U-Boot only reads the kernel FIT).
0003-arm-dts-rk3506-raise-SFC-to-80-MHz-add-rockchip-max-.patch
# WPEN per transfer (BIT29) — vendor parity, mirror of linux 0006. U-Boot only
# reads the kernel FIT (reliable w/ DLL tuning) so this is belt-and-suspenders.
0004-spi-rockchip_sfc-set-WPEN-per-transfer-vendor-parity.patch
